1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,660
When someone pulls up in a

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:04,086
three-hundred-thousand-dollar Ferrari,

3
00:00:04,086 --> 00:00:05,873
strangers stare at the hood,

4
00:00:05,873 --> 00:00:08,172
and mentally erase the person behind

5
00:00:08,172 --> 00:00:08,810
the wheel.

6
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:10,928
Working as a teenage hotel valet

7
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:11,920
in Los Angeles,

8
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:14,501
author Morgan Housel discovered the Man

9
00:00:14,501 --> 00:00:15,758
in the Car Paradox:

10
00:00:15,758 --> 00:00:18,802
onlookers never think the driver is admirable;

11
00:00:18,802 --> 00:00:20,920
they picture themselves driving.

12
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,579
That makes debt-fueled status symbols one

13
00:00:23,579 --> 00:00:25,395
of the worst trades in human

14
00:00:25,395 --> 00:00:26,109
psychology.

15
00:00:26,109 --> 00:00:28,962
You sacrifice real financial freedom chasing

16
00:00:28,962 --> 00:00:31,427
respect from strangers who aren't even

17
00:00:31,427 --> 00:00:32,400
looking at you.

18
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,012
If your true goal is genuine admiration,

19
00:00:35,012 --> 00:00:36,840
build it through competence,

20
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:37,623
reliability,

21
00:00:37,623 --> 00:00:38,211
kindness,

22
00:00:38,211 --> 00:00:39,386
and quiet mastery,

23
00:00:39,386 --> 00:00:42,520
assets no dealership lease can ever counterfeit.

24
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,554
Before any status purchase,

25
00:00:44,554 --> 00:00:46,889
ask whether you would still buy

26
00:00:46,889 --> 00:00:48,771
it on an island with zero

27
00:00:48,771 --> 00:00:49,600
spectators.
